& [RequiredSurface]
  + introduce one separate safe-Rust effect-free library named cantor_sop_inspect_wire
  + accept one bounded caller-supplied byte slice containing exactly one strict JSON request envelope
  + fix the envelope operation to semantic_inspect and carry one published InspectionRequest without semantic translation
  + return one bounded deterministic JSON response envelope whose status is exactly succeeded or refused
  + on success carry the exact published InspectionResult; on refusal carry only one bounded code and message; never carry both result and fault
  + seal the response envelope with a domain-separated digest and provide exact response replay validation
  + preserve nested inspection request validation bounds results faults ordering pagination lineage and non-authority without drift
  + make malformed unknown duplicate trailing oversized unsupported-operation and cross-field-invalid outer requests deterministic refusals
  + expose no stdin stdout file path socket service MCP LSP process environment clock random provider model or mutation API
  + leave a future one-shot stdin/stdout executable as a separately governed effect boundary over this pure codec

& [Acceptance]
  + the same valid request bytes always produce the same exact successful response bytes
  + nested semantic inspection output is byte-for-value identical to direct published kernel execution
  + every governed nested refusal becomes one stable refused response without partial success
  + outer response substitution omission digest or success-fault exclusivity tampering refuses replay
  + focused debug overflow-checked release exact workspace warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host custody formation and evidence gates pass before publication

& [NonAuthority]
  + wire means an in-memory request-response representation and does not mean a reader writer pipe terminal process service or transport
  + logical paths remain caller-supplied attribution labels and never authorize host access
  + no filesystem read or write SQLite persistence cache index context expansion ranking LSP MCP stdin stdout network process provider model inference installation update remote machine merge publication or external effect
  + no byte from C:\Project\Cantor is modified staged normalized copied back or deleted

& [ProcessingState]
  + preserved_unprocessed_SJS_required
